<title>RUSSIA: Russia to resume PGM exports in July - Tass.</title>
<headline>Russia to resume PGM exports in July - Tass.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's state precious metals export agency, Almazjuvelirexport, will resume exports of platinum group metals (PGMs) this month, Itar-Tass news agency quoted a Finance Ministry official as saying on Monday.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Japanese traders said last week Almazjuvelirexport had informed them that long-delayed shipments of platinum and palladium would resume around July 10.  </p>
<p>Russia is the world's top palladium supplier and second largest platinum supplier, with Japan the leading consumer of both metals.</p>
<p>Markets have been worried over Russia's protracted absence from the market and varying statements on when exports would resume.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
